      "round_summary": "Round 1 fix: two DUT bugs. (1) FSM state encoding: replaced `Enum(3)` (binary 0,1,2) with explicit one-hot values `sInit=001`, `sAnalisReq=010`, `sAssegna=100` so `assertOneHot(stato,\"fsm_state_one_hot\")` holds — state 0 (2'b00) had zero bits set, violating one-hot. (2) Stale grant: added `.otherwise{grant:=0.U}` on the `when(fu1||fu2||fu3||fu4)` block in `sAssegna` so grant is cleared when no follow-up registers are pending, fixing `grant3_requires_fu1` and all homologous grant assertions (`grant0_requires_fu4`, `grant1_requires_fu3`, `grant2_requires_fu2`). All 4 grant assertion labels preserved. All assertion labels preserved unchanged.",
